Q1. What is the difference between the Watch Window and the Locals Window?

Interview Ready Answer

The Locals window automatically displays all variables available in the current execution scope. The Watch window displays only the variables or expressions that the developer explicitly adds for continuous monitoring during debugging.

Definition

Locals Window

• Automatically displays all local variables in the current scope.

Watch Window

• Displays only developer-selected variables or expressions.

Purpose

Locals Window

• View all variables available in the current scope.
• Understand the current state of program execution.

Watch Window

• Monitor important variables continuously.
• Observe value changes across breakpoints and execution steps.

======================================================================

Q2. What is the purpose of the Watch Window?

Interview Ready Answer

The Watch window is used to continuously monitor specific variables or expressions that the developer explicitly adds during debugging. It helps developers observe how selected values change as the program executes.

Definition

The Watch window monitors selected variables or expressions during debugging.

Purpose

• Track important variables.
• Observe value changes during execution.
• Avoid searching for variables repeatedly.
• Simplify debugging of complex applications.

